        <p>2ND TEAMS. Played at Winnington Park on Saturday. Reoult,. to Causeway won 7 events to 5 (one not played), 16 se"lod 15, and 133 games to 142. Messrs C E B H Massink defeated 111essr3 Evanson and Pickering, '0.6 6-5 and 7-5 ; Messrs Maltby and Brocklehurst ,pd and 7-5 ; and Messrs Dobell and Postles, 3-6, 6.„l„lrer 6-4 ; Messrs J Cox and H Bibby, lost to Messrs r",1,1e• jog, 4-6 and 2-6, detested Me3srs Maltby and E,r°A-apd burst, 2 6, 6-2 and 6-2 ; and Dobell and Postles, 6-1 ; Messrs W Green and W J Isaac lost to Ire Maltby and Brocklehurst, 3-6, 6.5 and 4 6 ; and Ntoe Dobell and Poetise, 3-6, 6-4 and 2-6 ; Misses E Jscg"-6-5 and Price defeated Misses M Dobell and Jones, and 6 4 ; and Misses E Dobell and Wilkinson, 6"';‘,t 6-2 ; Misses Horton and D Isaac lost to Misse'.o.(l Dobell and Jones, 3-6 and 1-6 and Misses E Dobell ° Wilkinson, 3-6 and 1-6. THE " POPLARS " TENNIS CLUB. kg' A new tennis court which has been provided bi James at the "Poplars " Lovely-lane, vas rec—The opened at the headquarters of the above club per' lawn is pleasantly situated and everything sPbeerl veining to the comfort of the members baying ,sfa a'l carefully attended to. a most enjoyable and soc , season is anticipated.</p>
        <p>THE CQACHING CLIJB MEET. The opening meet of the Coaching Club, held in Hyde Park, proved that the popularity of the four-in-hand is on the increase, despite the motor. The meet was ene of the largest seen fo,r many years, and a huge crowd, in motor, on horseback, and afoct, gathered to watch the liana" some teams drive off to Burlingham.</p>
