        <p>?Pc' There was a fine crowd of habitues at tbe d tbei and Hippodrome on Monday evening, an'one.ili popularity of the Friars Green house of entel -aertit seems to increase each week uuder the able nn" this pob direction of Mr. Turpin. The programme le is nicely varied and wall-sustained by a company of artistes. One of the turns we lik—„ccli&amp; was that of the Ellesmere troupe of trick w-tolin) three ladies and two men who performed itotool, or Teats on the wheel with the utmost precinit° grace, notwithstanding the circumscribe° 1000 e of a theatre stage. Cycling, in their soge seems to have reached quite the la!„t tt'if of development. A novel item bill is that inrroduced by the Permane Bros. origl9o of" The Nightingale's Courtship." OPeni`ig sample of neat comedy juggling, these tyl° teeeie clowns, dressed up in costume supposed to llostre Mr. and Mrs. Nightingale, proceeded to courtship between the song-birds by marvellol2 mimicry of bird-notes. Their uncommon °le° One„ef recognised by a volume of hearty app,l3tte'coef the leading turns is the sporting skit Huntsman 'by Queen and Le Brun. The beet boTlf i in this item was provided by the pantonnine,ttifp• , which indulged in grotesque antics that 50,040 , compelled laughter. The work of Harr,' 0 ionye, 0 Oro( as the Cockney Huntsman was t°•,,l3t burlesqued, and much of his patter nlirprel3e'of 1 rewritten with advantage. Clara Coverdal° tra. ope an exceptionally well-drilled and expert ofy child dancers in the Nine Dainty I)°ts''. g o°so responsible for a pleasing vocal and danc,„l3,o9r3dl' " The Gypsies' Revels." Charles 130ebY BF:j J3o."fig comedian with moderate success,and Beale an partileo way put in treamendous exertion in their „ 019 duo, American style. Cora C ,tine efi • originality in her polylot scena whichairatlevt°o.,ol:oo.9,o, lightning changes of dress and ch variety of songs which take well with tne The interval is well-employed by ;riddlg Mr. ,e 0011 orchestra and in the prebentation 