        <head>BOWLING NOTES.</head>
        <p>BOWLING NOTES.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTQN AND DISTRICT CLUB CHAMPIONSHIP. Tbera was a large amount of interest centred in the return games in the first round of the Warrington and vsoataricus %strict Associaticn Club Championship played on the greens on Saturday afternoon. There were Theegood games witnessed, and notable wins recorded. Weather conditions were all that could be desired. a ° ugh many cf the greens were on the heavy side.</p>
        <p>Afte LIBERAL CLUB V. CEMETERY (No 1.) r having won by 4G points on the Church-street K7n on the previous Saturday the Cemetery men were I 33,, 1:4 confidence when they had the return visit to the li;reY-street sward. The Liberals, however, are no oiitearn, and not to be easily reckoned with on their wer-„‘Rnd, and although they lost on the aggregate they Alpe" .I"Ponsible for a very creditable disolay of the pe?":1 game on Saturday, which they won by seven szer:lB. This reduced the majority of the Church-street cre;i;°lll Z. 3 to 46, and the achievement reflects great to" the Liberal trundlers, for their opponents are ered one of the best teams in the competition. The</p>
        <p>811 i;." caPtain of the Cemetery team T Harrisou had senola Work cut out to defeat W Taylor and be only In,e,sratilished this feat by one point after 33 ends bad 10ti: contested. The going was fairly even up to the he n,„erl(l when Taylor led by 7-6. In the nest six ends roain",B,oll favourite land and ran his lead to 14-7. He led ?;tl„ed the advantage up to the 27th end when he 'eoeCh:l-16. A double and a single in the next two r'ad-f° gave Harrison the lead of 19-17 but on the 38th 19 , akYlor got a couple of beauties and made the score 13r1Pt-heg* At the 32nd end the score was 20 each and -'3 next length Harrison gained his one by inches. Diut 0 a'lltith (Liberals) was off his pitch in the first •eei v.! his encounter with A J Jones and at the ninth niett:',e Cemetery man had a lead of 11-5. In the next eod lengths Daintith made headway and at the 22nd dowl the .. Players peeled with 17 ea ;b. Two neat Inv"? in the next three lengths and a single for Jones "ie Bewsey-street trundler the game by 21-18. that ere Nit. ere is one man who knows the peculiarities of ' C.e, lberal Green it is B Webb, and although on the Green he was beaten by five points, the Set' noPporters were confident ttat he would make "riC,3,en his own soil, and this he did, for be disposed Woods by 21-17, although the game panned out 58d ,'erigthri. Webb was always ahead from the first Nife;.:tbe 2lst end he bad a lead of 19-8. However, liddein be could get his two points his opponent had l' fe-n"ve singles and two doubles and eventually lost r chalk,. la tk -- N f" Meantime the Liberal team secretary,F Walker, tolar„ing viry badly in his game with T Bolton. m[tpe - 18 one of the best trandlers the Cemetery team ON got and from the first he took the lead,the strange- "lots °f,,tbe green troubling him very little. Walker, r. could not get his measure or the score would - 'een quite of a-different nature. A, n, INk I;'"a° e made up for his defeat of the previous ticN. Y ,ir,disposing of