        <p>At Ordination. oun,ter Cathedral on Sunday, the Rev. Edward staff-01'15.A., University of London, a member of the the Boteler Grammar School and curate at CheePteern.bali, was ordained priest by the Bishop of I sr net Necessarily " Bad People." After PeEzti„ ~,00ndemning the Welsh Disestablishment pro- beem".' "rford "Parish Magazine" continues : Now, Pe,oPle are opposed to us it does not mean that ° 'neeti;e ad people; end as for their motives these e at they are doing what is iaccounted for by them to God alone. If they welta!,thtionest and right, their '!u good. But there are those who do not share of the wisdom of disestablishment nor of the • ?f disendowment, end it is for us who think spell disaster to the nation to fight for what shrive to be wise and right. Holy Trinity Church. ,Presentation to the Apparitor.. sPasri, °Qn Jefferson, who has held the position of ttltio'cl at Holy Trinity Church for thirty years, was Puru'ivaY evening presented by the congregation with 'ouse.ef gold, an illuminated address and a book, scrib. In morocco, containing the names of thesub- -441 kr„s• The Vicar (Rev E C E Carleton) r resided, 's Carleton made the presentation. 1, Parish Church New Vestry. 124:°111, eetines of the Parish Church Councillhave been the first (says the Parish Church Magazine) kgrip"° amended tenders for the new vestry for between lot °1 £7OO were discussed, but as the architect was 14„%t:',„esent the meeting was adjourned. At the last after full consideration, it was decided to 44te 1-4 further action until:the result of the parochial th: the autumn was made known. The postponement t,,werk was a great disappointment to us, but it Os ive-,,"„that with but half the amount required in hand not be wise to incur such an expenditure as oett,-,'hitect tells us is absolutely necessary to build Sof such a size as we need, and of such a I,suchrisp.r:ti Pel!jses to be in harmony with and a credit to the oChurch. In the meantime we shall see beath: u hand