        <p>EDUCATION ACT, 1902. CHESHIRE LOCAL EDUCATION AUTHORITY. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN in accordance with the provisions of Section 8 (I) and (2) of the Education Act, 1902, that we, the undersigned, propose to enlarge the Halton Grammar School, situated in the township of Halton, in the Rural District of Runcorn. in the County of Chester, by providing additional accommodation for about 140 children. The Board of Education consider this enlargement to he such as to amount to the provision of a new School. The said School Is conducted ea a Voluntary School or School not provided by the Local Education Authority under the conditions prescribed in Section 7 of the said Act, and religions instruction is gives in school hours in accordance with the provisions of Section 7 (2) of the Elementary Education Act 1870, and in conformity with the doctrines of the Church of England. The School will he available for the following area :—The TOWNSHIPS OF HALTON, NORTON, STOCKHAM, and CLIFTON, in the RURAL DISTRICT OF RUNCORN. The Managers of any existing School, or the Local Education Authority, or any ten ratepayers in the area for which it is proposed to provide the School, may appeal against this proposal by a letter addressed to the Secretary, Board of Education, Whitehall, London, S.W., which should reach him within three months from the date of this notice. R. M. BROOKE. C. L. EVANS. Dated 2nd Mav, 1912. R. G. GREENHAM, Vicar.</p>
