        <p>Penketn. FUNERAL OF MRS. JAMES HOWARD.—The funeral took place at Sankey Cemetery on ruesday afternoon of the late Mrs. James Howard, of Heath-road,Penketh, who passed easy on Saturday morning after a long illness. She was born in Penketh, was sixty years of , age, and had lived in the district all her life. Orford. THANKSGIVING SERVICE.—Snecial services were held at Orford Church, on Sunday, as a thanksgiving for the paving off of the debt on the Church. Special psalms and hymns were suns. The preacher at all the services. 10.30, 3 o'clock and 6.30, was the vicar, the Key G Vale Owen. Woolston. CAILD DRoWNFD IN A POND.—A sad drowning fitality occurred on Thursday evening. Oswald Platt (aged 5), oi Moss-lane, Woolston, was playing with other children on the banks of a pond by the side of Long Barn-road. when he fell in and drowned before help could be obtained. PC. Kay recovered the body, and Dr. Bennett was soon on the scene, but all attempts at resuscitation were of no avail.</p>
