        <p>A BAD WARRINGTON MAN'S WORD Mr. H. Law, of Chesham, Whitefield Road, Stockton Heath, Warrington, who is well known amongst the farmers of the district, says :—"Having used Doan's Backache Kidney Pills, off and on, for about two years, I can speak with the utmost confidence as to their efficacy in the relief of lumbago. "After using the pills I have invari- ably found them effective in a remark- ably short time, removing the pains after a few doses. " I have frequently mentioned this remedy to friends similarly troubled, and subsequently their testimony has agreed with my own experience—the pills having been, almost without excep- tion, as successful in their cases as in mine. (Signed) H. LAW."</p>
